<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS1" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.1 </span>Why did you prefer your highest ranked method? Please elaborate and compare the methods for both the individual and social settings.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS2" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.2 </span>Which methods did you feel in control while using? Why/why not?</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS3" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.3 </span>Which method had the most appropriate bite timing? Elaborate on why it had the most appropriate timing and compare it to the other methods.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS4" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.4 </span>What cues do you think a caregiver/you use to know when to feed a care recipient/yourself a bite?</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS5" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.5 </span>Which method was closest to how a caregiver/you would perform this task? Please elaborate on why.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS6" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.6 </span>Were the glasses comfortable to wear while eating? If not, please explain.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS13.SSS7" title="In A.13. Phase 2 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.13.7 </span>Was the throat microphone comfortable to wear while eating? If not, please explain.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A1.SS14" title="In Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14 </span>Phase 3 Qualitative Responses</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS1" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.1 </span>Did you like this bite timing method for this setting? Why or why not?</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS2" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.2 </span>Did you feel in control while using the robot with this bite timing method for this setting? Why/why not?</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS3" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.3 </span>Did this method have appropriate bite timing for this setting? Elaborate on why/why not.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS4" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.4 </span>What cues do you think a caregiver uses to know when to feed you a bite for this setting?</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS5" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.5 </span>Was this method close to how a caregiver would perform this task for this setting? Please elaborate on why.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS6" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.6 </span>Were the glasses comfortable to wear while eating for this setting? If not, please explain.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#A1.SS14.SSS7" title="In A.14. Phase 3 Qualitative Responses ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">A.14.7 </span>Was the throat microphone comfortable to wear while eating for this setting? If not, please explain.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
