</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We visually show the study setup for the three phases in Fig. <a href="#acmlabel5" title="Figure A1 ‣ A.3. Study Setup Additional Details ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A1</span></a> and directly compare them in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table A1 ‣ A.3. Study Setup Additional Details ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following questions and Likert items were asked to participants after testing each method in the Phase 2 study:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Would you consider the timing of the bites appropriate? (Yes/No)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">How was the bite timing of this method on average? (Very Early, Early, Slightly Early, Right Time, Slightly Late, Late, Very Late)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L1: I was not distracted by this bite timing method.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L2: I felt in control of the robot with this method.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L3: The robot understands when I want a bite.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L4: The robot moved at the appropriate moments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L5: This bite timing method is seamless.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L6: This bite timing method required no mental workload.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L7: This bite timing method required no physical workload.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">L8: For social dining only: The robot allowed me to have natural conversation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At the end of the Phase 2 study, the participants answer the following qualitative questions:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Why did you prefer your highest ranked method? Please elaborate and compare the methods for both the individual and social settings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which methods did you feel in control while using? Why or why not?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which method had the most appropriate bite timing? Elaborate on why it had the most appropriate timing and compare it to the other methods.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What cues do you think a caregiver or you use to know when to feed a care recipient or yourself a bite?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which method was closest to how a caregiver or you would perform this task? Please elaborate on why.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Were the glasses comfortable to wear while eating? If not, please explain.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Was the throat microphone comfortable to wear while eating? If not, please explain.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Social Dining Conversation Topics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to Ondras et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ondras et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, we utilize the following conversation starters for the social dining portion of the study:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Who is your favorite singer and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What are you studying?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What is your favorite food and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What is your favorite color and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Do you give back or volunteer with any organizations?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What are your favorite writers and books?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Do you have any pets and if so, what are they?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What sports do you play or watch and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What is your favorite movie and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Who is your favorite actor and why?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which languages do you speak and which ones do you want to learn?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What was your favorite vacation?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What are your hobbies?</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To foster a more natural conversation, we encourage participants to ask the researcher questions in return. Additionally, we have the researcher eat food to simulate a shared meal experience.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5. </span>Wizard of Oz Guidelines</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To mitigate participant suspicion, the researcher uses a video feed from the RealSense camera displayed on the companion robot to get a clear view of the participant’s face during data collection. These guidelines are listed in order of priority as sometimes cues can conflict; for example, the person may still be chewing while also glancing at the robot to indicate they want another bite.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.1. </span>Individual</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Listed in order of priority, so in the case of a conflict, higher ones should be adhered to before lower ones:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant starts glancing toward the robot or the camera</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Participant’s body language or other forms of communication indicate they do not want the bite (e.g., leaning backwards, turning their head away from the spoon, etc.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant is not chewing</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant is giving indication that they are almost done chewing, such as:</p>
<ul id="A1.I4.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visibly or audibly chewing significantly more lightly than previously</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Licking their mouth area</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visibly or audibly swallowing</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Participant is chewing</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.2. </span>Social</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Listed in order of priority, so in the case of a conflict, higher ones should be adhered to before lower ones:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Participant’s body language or other forms of communication indicate they do not want the bite (e.g., leaning backwards, turning their head away from the spoon, etc.)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant is giving indication that they are almost done talking, such as:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Posing a question to the dining partner</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Trailing off</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Participant is talking</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Dining partner is giving indication that they are almost done talking, such as:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Posing a question to the participant</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Trailing off</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Dining partner is talking</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant is not chewing</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(7)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Move forward: Participant is giving indication that they are almost done chewing, such as:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5.i7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visibly or audibly chewing significantly more lightly than previously</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Licking their mouth area</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visibly or audibly swallowing</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(8)</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stop: Participant is chewing</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6. </span>Food Options</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Phase 1 studies, we allow participants to pick a soft, medium, and hard food and an additional wildcard food from any of the following 3 categories to fill the 4 bowls of the Obi robot:</p>
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Soft: yogurt, applesauce, tomato soup</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Medium: rice, mac and cheese, corn, mashed potatoes</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hard: pretzels, cheerios, granola, goldfish</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For Phase 2 studies, we all participants to pick 2 medium and 2 hard foods. We exclude soft foods from this study as there is increased risk of food spillage due to feeding from the side. The foods chosen by participants in Phase 1 and Phase 2 are provided in Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table A2 ‣ A.6. Food Options ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A2</span></a> and Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table A3 ‣ A.6. Food Options ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A3</span></a>. For both Phase 1 and Phase 2 studies, a small display monitor is placed on the table in front of the user to indicate which bowl the robot will be scooping from next. The fruits chosen by participants in Phase 3 are provided in the main text.</p>
</div>
