<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7. </span>Participant Demographics</h3>

<section id="A1.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.7.1. </span>Phase 1</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to the demographics detailed in the main text, participants were asked how much experience they have with controlling a robot and their level of hunger. Three additional participants were excluded, two because they took very few bites as they were not hungry during the session, and one due to sensor connection issues. We visually show participant demographics from our Phase 1 studies in Fig <a href="#acmlabel6" title="Figure A2 ‣ A.7.1. Phase 1 ‣ A.7. Participant Demographics ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03910v1/phase1_dem.svg" id="A1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/136;" width="476" height="136" aria-label="TODO"><p>TODO</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A2. </span>Phase 1 (n=14) Demographics<span id="acmlabel6" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">TODO</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.7.2. </span>Phase 2</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the Phase 1 study, participants were also asked how much experience they have with controlling a robot and their level of hunger. We visually show participant demographics from our Phase 2 studies in Fig <a href="#acmlabel7" title="Figure A3 ‣ A.7.3. Phase 3 ‣ A.7. Participant Demographics ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.7.3. </span>Phase 3</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The majority of Phase 3 demographics information is presented in the main text in Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4. Phase 3: Evaluation with Individuals with Motor Impairments ‣ 3. Methods ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. Additionally, both participants with motor impairments indicated their level of hunger was “Moderately Hungry”.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03910v1/phase2_dem.svg" id="A1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/136;" width="476" height="136" aria-label="TODO"><p>TODO</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A3. </span>Phase 2 (n=15) Demographics<span id="acmlabel7" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">TODO</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8. </span>Metrics using Different Fixed Assertiveness Thresholds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include the accuracy and nMCC metrics for fixed assertiveness threshold values from 4 seconds to 8 seconds in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table A4 ‣ A.8. Metrics using Different Fixed Assertiveness Thresholds ‣ Appendix A Appendices ‣ WAFFLE: A Wearable Approach to Bite Timing Estimation in Robot-Assisted Feeding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A4</span></a>. We find that the threshold of 6 seconds outperforms all other threshold values.</p>
</div>
